WEBVTT

00:00:03.530 --> 00:00:04.980
I told you!

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:11.290
If you really want to write that genre,
then you should just do it by yourself!

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:15.490
Frankly, aren't you just pushing things on us?

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:19.140
We're not really that serious about this.

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:21.060
Besides, it's just a doujinshi.

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:24.000
Why are you so strict with the deadlines?

00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:27.600
It's not fun at all if you're
going to be so unreasonable.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:29.000
That's how it is.

00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:31.500
Well, do as you like.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:32.920
Let's go.

00:02:33.350 --> 00:02:35.420
All right, that's it.

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:39.150
Hey, what did you get for four?

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:41.640
Put your pens down!

00:02:42.650 --> 00:02:46.640
Turn your papers over and pass them forward.

00:02:47.110 --> 00:02:51.690
If your score is below 30,
you'll have to take supplementary classes.

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:56.400
It's already too late.

00:02:56.830 --> 00:02:59.150
Oh man, I'll probably have to take them.

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:01.740
Do we have any club activities today?

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:04.160
Enough already!

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:18.160
Sumi-chan!

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:22.800
Do you want to go over the answers together—

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:26.180
Ah, Aoi-san.

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:30.720
Have you thought about what
we discussed the other day?

00:03:31.530 --> 00:03:33.940
The other day... about what?

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:35.520
This!

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:39.390
The "YuriFest" with all the latest yuri works at sale!

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:44.470
As the missionaries of Orino Masaka,
we have to set up a place for her goods!

00:03:44.470 --> 00:03:47.870
It'd be the perfect time to publish our own work, if only we had the money.

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:50.530
Let's do it!

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:51.470
Anyway, since it's your first doujinshi,

00:03:51.470 --> 00:03:53.540
Don't run away! Help me!

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:53.620
She's your brother's fan!

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:56.380
I hope Masaka-oneesama will find it interesting.

00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:57.130
No, you can't get too close to her.

00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:59.420
Ah, but don't worry too much.

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:02.220
If it gets out that my brother is Orino Masaka,

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:03.930
there'll be serious trouble!

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:05.800
It'll be fine. With his skills,

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:07.350
they won't mind that he's actually a man.

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:09.430
Sumi-chan, you don't understand the fans!

00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:11.390
The passionate feelings of adolescents can

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:13.270
easily transform into negative energy!

00:04:13.270 --> 00:04:14.560
You worry too much!

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:15.690
Have faith in your brother!

00:04:15.690 --> 00:04:17.940
Those are two unrelated matters!

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:19.980
The editorial board thought it'd be better for the fans

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:22.200
for the author to remain an enigmatic woman.

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:24.110
You mustn't expose the truth!

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:25.740
Aren't you just deceiving the fans?

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:27.530
No! We're only giving them hope!

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:28.530
Hiding the truth from their eyes!

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:32.740
I'm amazed that they can communicate like that.

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:37.540
And why doesn't Big Brow
over there notice anything?

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:51.550
All right! Time to get home
and work on the manuscript.

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:54.560
Time to make up for the break!

00:04:58.030 --> 00:04:59.570
It's so hot.

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:02.530
Where are you going to work over the summer break?

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:04.320
I wonder...

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:08.280
Think there's a job that'll pay 1,000 yen an hour just to sit in an air-conditioned room?

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:09.330
In your dreams.

00:05:12.760 --> 00:05:17.080
Go right ahead and enjoy
your summer of intemperance.

00:05:24.850 --> 00:05:27.040
As for my summer, I'll have...

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:33.850
...made a doujinshi with Murasame-san.

00:05:34.780 --> 00:05:37.350
Slept over at Murasame-san's place.

00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:40.610
Participated in an event.

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:43.610
Gone to the beach and the mountains.

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:47.610
Things like that!

00:05:48.630 --> 00:05:51.080
Welcome back, Azusa.

00:05:51.880 --> 00:05:52.740
I'm back—

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:54.700
Could you watch the store for a while?

00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:56.870
Why?

00:05:56.870 --> 00:05:58.880
Where's Mother?

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:01.570
She's visiting Grandma at the hospital.

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:04.090
You have time now that you're
done with your tests, right?

00:06:04.090 --> 00:06:04.640
I have things to do too!

00:06:04.640 --> 00:06:06.670
I'm counting on you!

00:06:06.670 --> 00:06:07.120
I have things to do too!

00:06:18.910 --> 00:06:21.400
Welcome, welcome!

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:31.370
Oh, well.

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:36.800
It's not like this place is quiet
in the afternoon anyway.

00:06:41.260 --> 00:06:47.420
Now that we have put the tests behind us,
we need to start thinking about our activities in earnest!

00:06:47.830 --> 00:06:50.640
Activities? What for?

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:53.010
Did the tests sap your wit, Murasame-kun?

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:55.060
I'm talking about the Girls' Club, of course!

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:57.430
You still haven't given up on that?

00:06:57.800 --> 00:07:01.440
"Giving up" isn't part of Tomoe-chan's vocabulary.

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:05.190
I suspect that it's lacking various other words as well.

00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:11.700
The application was rejected,
and Yamasaki Akemi-kun has vanished.

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:14.820
Where in the world has Akemi-chan gone?

00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:19.040
She vanished without a trace, huh?

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:21.750
Truly, she's just like a ghost member.

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:25.100
That was some clever wordplay, Tomoe-chan!

00:07:25.100 --> 00:07:29.220
We of the Girls' Club now face the greatest challenge since our founding!

00:07:29.580 --> 00:07:30.970
Already?

00:07:30.970 --> 00:07:37.160
At this rate, we won't be able to realize our dream of a girls-only time after school!

00:07:38.240 --> 00:07:40.230
How is that different from what we're doing now?

00:07:40.670 --> 00:07:43.100
How many times do I have
to tell you, Murasame-kun?

00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:45.650
High school is all about club activities!

00:07:45.650 --> 00:07:46.750
I understand.

00:07:48.870 --> 00:07:52.740
I thoroughly understand that nothing I say gets through to you.

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:54.990
That's one of the good things
about Tomoe-chan!

00:07:55.210 --> 00:07:56.700
That's good?

00:07:56.700 --> 00:08:01.000
I tried to recruit Torioi-kun again, but...

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:03.750
"I must politely decline! Ha ha ha!"

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:05.210
...is what she said.

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:06.990
Just when did you...

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:10.510
Anyway, don't bother Kiyori-chan.

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:15.010
We'll think of other ways to attract new members.

00:08:15.010 --> 00:08:19.020
For now, I have a plan to strengthen our bonds.

00:08:21.240 --> 00:08:22.520
What are we going to do?

00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:25.270
It's summer!

00:08:25.570 --> 00:08:28.970
When you think of summer,
it's got to be a training camp!

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:41.790
Murasame-san's home was such a splendid mansion.

00:08:42.230 --> 00:08:44.600
She even had a housekeeper.

00:08:46.010 --> 00:08:49.470
I'm sure she has a summer house too.

00:08:51.350 --> 00:08:54.880
What should I do if she were to invite me?

00:08:55.690 --> 00:08:59.140
Look! The starry sky is so beautiful.

00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:03.810
Yeah, it's as if the two of us are floating in space!

00:09:10.090 --> 00:09:11.030
As if!

00:09:11.030 --> 00:09:15.060
Geez, I might even try writing
an original this summer!

00:09:15.790 --> 00:09:18.070
Um, excuse me.

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:22.280
That could be great!

00:09:29.430 --> 00:09:33.370
Rather than a derivative, it'll be an original work!

00:09:40.230 --> 00:09:44.810
Still, I wonder if it's too obvious whom the characters are modeled after.

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:49.370
Just how does one write an original?

00:09:51.830 --> 00:09:53.690
It's my first time.

00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:59.030
Perhaps it would be safer to write a derivative.

00:10:07.680 --> 00:10:10.040
No, that's wrong.

00:10:16.140 --> 00:10:18.800
I might not be able to write it well,

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:23.510
but if I do my best, I'm sure Murasame-san will be inspired too!

00:10:25.400 --> 00:10:29.310
Most importantly, this is the first novel I'll be writing with a friend!

00:10:30.300 --> 00:10:32.310
I want to give it my best!

00:10:36.460 --> 00:10:38.030
Is Azusa in her room?

00:10:38.030 --> 00:10:39.410
Yeah.

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:42.490
Wasn't she done with the tests already?

00:10:42.490 --> 00:10:46.490
It's probably that doujinshi thing.

00:10:48.220 --> 00:10:51.670
That's right. She was happy to find a friend who shared her interests.

00:10:52.510 --> 00:10:54.600
She really had me worried.

00:10:55.180 --> 00:10:58.710
Even though she's in high school,
she didn't seem to have any friends.

00:11:03.110 --> 00:11:06.700
She seems to be fine now, though.

00:11:20.940 --> 00:11:24.620
It's been decided that the training camp will be on August 6th.

00:11:24.620 --> 00:11:27.540
Hold it! Are we actually doing this?

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:29.310
I did tell you.

00:11:30.430 --> 00:11:35.670
You may be the top student in our grade, but your memory is deplorably deficient.

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:38.800
As a member, you need to be more conscious.

00:11:38.800 --> 00:11:45.680
The "Planning Club" doesn't need a training camp!

00:11:46.050 --> 00:11:48.320
I told you, it's the "Girls' Club."

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:51.690
We should clean up properly, everyone.

00:11:51.950 --> 00:11:55.360
You can't simply decide things on your own.

00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:57.520
I have plans myself.

00:11:58.580 --> 00:12:00.150
Murasame-kun.

00:12:00.150 --> 00:12:01.070
What is it?

00:12:01.370 --> 00:12:03.410
Our destination is the beach!

00:12:03.410 --> 00:12:04.700
Use your imagination.

00:12:05.070 --> 00:12:06.720
When you think of the beach...

00:12:13.430 --> 00:12:16.950
Sumi-chan!

00:12:20.770 --> 00:12:24.890
That's delusion, not imagination.

00:12:29.240 --> 00:12:35.600
W-Well, a camp sounds good; it's summer, after all!

00:12:36.030 --> 00:12:37.650
Sumi-chan?

00:12:37.650 --> 00:12:39.480
So simple.

00:12:56.350 --> 00:12:57.790
The beach?

00:12:57.790 --> 00:12:58.790
Sounds good!

00:12:59.240 --> 00:13:01.630
Would you like to come with us, Torioi-kun?

00:13:01.630 --> 00:13:03.090
Can I?

00:13:03.090 --> 00:13:06.590
I'll go if it doesn't clash with any other club activities.

00:13:06.590 --> 00:13:09.310
But I wonder if the swimsuit
from last year will fit me.

00:13:09.830 --> 00:13:10.930
Die!

00:13:10.930 --> 00:13:12.430
Well, then...

00:13:12.920 --> 00:13:16.770
...let's go shopping for one after school tomorrow.

00:13:16.770 --> 00:13:18.940
Yeah, let's do that.

00:13:20.370 --> 00:13:22.440
You're so transparent.

00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:23.440
What?!

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:23.940
Whatever!

00:13:24.200 --> 00:13:25.040
What do you mean by "transparent"?!

00:13:25.040 --> 00:13:26.450
Stop fighting...
What do you mean by "transparent"?!

00:13:28.840 --> 00:13:31.580
You're still delusional.

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:32.620
I am not!

00:13:32.620 --> 00:13:33.510
I know all about it!

00:13:33.510 --> 00:13:36.000
I bet you do it all night too!

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:41.870
I'm sure she'll be surprised when I show her the finished manuscript.

00:13:56.570 --> 00:14:01.230
She might even be inspired to write an original work of her own.

00:14:04.120 --> 00:14:05.990
Hold on...

00:14:05.990 --> 00:14:08.990
If I do this, it won't be a novel
about Masaka-oneesama.

00:14:11.300 --> 00:14:12.990
Oh, well.

00:14:14.340 --> 00:14:17.500
Oh, I'm so excited!

00:14:19.890 --> 00:14:25.290
Even though summer vacation hasn't even started yet,
I'm already having this much fun!

00:14:35.860 --> 00:14:36.770
It's done.

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:39.140
It's done! It's finally done!

00:14:39.140 --> 00:14:42.720
My very own first original work!

00:14:44.450 --> 00:14:46.780
Oh my, what should I do?

00:14:46.780 --> 00:14:47.900
I can't believe it!

00:14:48.160 --> 00:14:51.780
With two columns and 1,200 characters a page,
it has a total of 50 pages!

00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:54.990
It might be impossible for me to make copies!

00:14:54.990 --> 00:14:56.290
Could it be?

00:14:56.700 --> 00:14:59.790
I'm on the path of adulthood!

00:15:01.550 --> 00:15:04.490
I'll think about that later.

00:15:07.230 --> 00:15:09.800
For now, I'll sleep for a while.

00:15:12.980 --> 00:15:16.310
School's in two hours, though.

00:15:17.150 --> 00:15:18.620
That's right...

00:15:19.660 --> 00:15:21.260
The title.

00:15:23.530 --> 00:15:25.720
What should I call it?

00:15:30.750 --> 00:15:32.510
Sunflowers...

00:15:33.180 --> 00:15:36.330
The Language of Sunflowers?

00:15:39.430 --> 00:15:43.290
I'm gazing at you.

00:15:47.220 --> 00:15:49.720
Was I supposed to do something?

00:15:50.980 --> 00:15:53.970
You don't... remember?

00:15:54.300 --> 00:15:56.100
Shortly after the test...

00:15:56.100 --> 00:15:58.470
Ah, that?

00:15:58.840 --> 00:16:02.850
I'm sorry, but I was still out of it
at the time due to the test.

00:16:03.210 --> 00:16:05.360
Okay, take your seats.

00:16:05.360 --> 00:16:07.110
I'm going to return your report cards.

00:16:07.110 --> 00:16:09.530
I'll see you afterwards!

00:16:10.290 --> 00:16:14.870
I guess no one calls them report cards these days.

00:16:33.060 --> 00:16:34.640
It's all right.

00:16:40.440 --> 00:16:41.770
I'm fine.

00:16:43.990 --> 00:16:45.400
I told you!

00:16:45.400 --> 00:16:46.770
Honestly...

00:16:46.770 --> 00:16:49.150
...it's just a doujinshi!

00:16:49.150 --> 00:16:52.350
Why are you so strict with the deadlines?

00:17:00.090 --> 00:17:01.780
Aoi-san?

00:17:08.560 --> 00:17:12.480
Don't be late, or I'll be berated too!

00:17:13.390 --> 00:17:15.150
When was it again?

00:17:17.110 --> 00:17:18.760
Nine o'clock.

00:17:18.760 --> 00:17:20.180
Wasn't it ten?

00:17:20.550 --> 00:17:22.390
That's when we open.

00:17:22.390 --> 00:17:24.770
Why at nine, then?

00:17:24.770 --> 00:17:29.200
We need to clean the store and get everything ready before we open.

00:17:34.620 --> 00:17:35.950
I'm fine.

00:17:41.170 --> 00:17:44.610
I guess Aoi-san really did go home.

00:17:44.930 --> 00:17:46.250
Murasame-kun.

00:18:31.530 --> 00:18:35.600
It's not like it's my first summer vacation alone.

00:18:46.700 --> 00:18:48.490
Welcome back, Azusa.

00:18:50.780 --> 00:18:53.100
What, were your grades bad?

00:18:53.480 --> 00:18:55.920
Dear, there's another order for beer.

00:18:55.920 --> 00:18:58.520
Oh, Azusa, welcome back.

00:18:58.520 --> 00:19:02.410
Ah, that event — what was it again?

00:19:03.070 --> 00:19:04.840
You're going with your friend, right?

00:19:04.840 --> 00:19:07.040
You should bring her over sometime.

00:19:07.890 --> 00:19:08.770
Yeah.

00:20:01.600 --> 00:20:03.110
This room's filthy as well.

00:20:03.590 --> 00:20:06.980
I guess people who like you
are all fools like this one.

00:20:11.700 --> 00:20:12.860
I...

00:20:14.030 --> 00:20:16.110
...did something horrible, didn't I?

00:20:18.180 --> 00:20:22.610
If you really believe that,
it'll be all right if you make up for it.

00:20:39.200 --> 00:20:41.300
Did I fall asleep?

00:20:43.010 --> 00:20:46.300
Oh no, the window was open.

00:20:46.950 --> 00:20:49.290
I wonder if the neighbors heard me crying.

00:20:57.320 --> 00:21:01.590
Murasame-san?

00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:06.750
I'm sorry.

00:21:11.150 --> 00:21:12.850
Murasame-san?!

00:21:12.850 --> 00:21:14.330
Why?!

00:23:02.210 --> 00:23:05.500
So, what did you have in mind for this book?

00:23:05.500 --> 00:23:09.110
Really, Murasame-san,
don't you even know that much?

00:23:09.390 --> 00:23:10.930
This!

00:23:10.930 --> 00:23:14.350
The "YuriFest" with all the latest yuri works at sale!

00:23:15.540 --> 00:23:20.350
Parodies, two-dimensional, three-dimensional, and other gems — truly a liberated yuri haven!

00:23:20.350 --> 00:23:23.720
It's held within the hallow grounds of Ariake, where no boy may set foot!

00:23:23.720 --> 00:23:27.210
It's a bi-annual festival for maidens!

00:23:32.340 --> 00:23:34.960
August... seventh?!

00:23:37.100 --> 00:23:38.350
We're at the beach next week!

00:23:38.350 --> 00:23:38.730
Yep!

00:23:38.730 --> 00:23:39.430
Isn't that nice.

00:23:39.430 --> 00:23:41.480
I got my license for days like this!

00:23:41.480 --> 00:23:42.230
Wonderful!

00:23:42.230 --> 00:23:43.860
I have a bad feeling about this, though.

00:23:44.360 --> 00:23:47.070
That's strange. The engine isn't...

00:23:47.070 --> 00:23:48.530
Go! Go!

00:23:48.530 --> 00:23:49.280
Are you all right?
